cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "U.S. Rapid Panel Resistance Marker Concordance Benchmark"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-24"
authors:
  - family-names: "Abdulwahab"
    given-names: "Fatima"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Dallas, Texas, USA"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-2298-8386"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/FatimaAbdulwahab/us-rapid-panel-amr-concordance"
url: "https://fatimaabdulwahab.github.io/us-rapid-panel-amr-concordance/"
abstract: >-
  An open isolate-level dataset pairing NCBI AMRFinderPlus resistance gene calls with submitted
  laboratory susceptibility results for U.S. human clinical isolates of Staphylococcus aureus,
  Enterococcus faecalis, Enterococcus faecium and the Enterobacterales, scored gene by gene for
  the targets that rapid blood culture panels report (mecA, mecC, vanA, vanB, KPC, NDM,
  OXA-48-like, VIM, IMP, CTX-M), with every discordant isolate classified by likely cause.
keywords:
  - antimicrobial resistance
  - rapid diagnostics
  - blood culture identification panel
  - AMRFinderPlus
  - genotype-phenotype concordance
  - carbapenemase
  - mecA
  - vanA
  - CTX-M
  - NCBI Pathogen Detection
